cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "amr-clonalshare: measuring how much of antimicrobial resistance travels with the clone"
abstract: >-
  Estimates the share of variance in an antimicrobial resistance phenotype
  that the lineages of a bacterial collection carry, from a lineage label and
  a susceptibility call or a recorded dilution, and refuses the estimate
  where the collection cannot support one. Two estimands are reported with
  their own intervals, a realised share for the collection in hand with an
  exact noncentral-F interval, and a superpopulation share for the species
  with a cluster-bootstrap interval, each behind a gate whose operating
  characteristics were measured against a known truth; the lineage label may
  be a sequence type, a core-genome or SNP cluster, or a serovar, so the same
  estimate can be read at two typing resolutions.
  A second family of outputs clusters one or more binary genotype layers (acquired antimicrobial-resistance
  determinants, virulence loci, capsule type) by similarity-network fusion, and
  reports the diagnostics that decide whether the resulting partition means
  anything: whether the largest cluster is the trait-absent stratum produced by
  the empty-union distance convention, whether tied affinities make the answer
  depend on input row order, whether the fusion collapsed onto a single layer,
  and whether the clusters are a clonal relabelling. Post-clustering inference
  uses multi-split feature splitting with a p-value merging rule valid for
  exchangeable, arbitrarily dependent p-values, and separates "there is
  structure" from "that structure is discrete" with a parametric bootstrap from
  a BIC-selected latent-trait continuum model with adaptive dimension checking
  and exact finite-bootstrap uncertainty. A five-level machine-readable claim
  ladder exposes every applicable gate and prevents a partition from being
  promoted directly to a biological archetype.
  A third family of outputs decomposes a difference in non-wild-type
  prevalence between two collections into a lineage-composition and a
  within-lineage rate component using the Kitagawa identity, with a calibrated
  estimability gate on shared lineage support, a test for lineage labels that
  are differentially and informatively missing, and Benjamini-Yekutieli
  control within each component family, valid whatever the dependence between
  agents, beside the effective number of independent agents. Prevalence is reported on both the isolate and the lineage scale.
  Ships two independently seeded positive controls, negative and adversarial
  controls, and documented Klebsiella pneumoniae and Streptococcus suis case
  studies in which statistical discreteness and biological interpretation are
  reported separately.
  A fourth family of outputs reads a susceptibility panel at its recorded
  resolution: a dichotomised call and a recorded dilution are both intervals on
  the log2 concentration scale and enter one interval likelihood, so the input
  mode changes how much an observation carries rather than what is estimated.
  Each share also carries an anytime-valid e-value, with false-discovery
  control across the panel that holds under arbitrary dependence between
  antimicrobials. The attribution is exercised outside the shipped cohorts on
  192 species-agent cells from 12 species of NCBI Pathogen Detection, each
  with a permuted-label control, and on 402 host-by-agent cells of animal
  surveillance at two typing resolutions.
